      "text": "Since $r$, $s$, and $t$ are the solutions to $x^3-5x^2+6x=9$, by Vieta's formulas we have the following relationships:\n\\begin{align\\*}\nr+s+t&=5,\\\\\nrs+st+tr&=6,\\\\\nrst&=-9.\\\\\n\\end{align\\*}\n\nWe want to compute $\\frac{rs}t + \\frac{st}r + \\frac{tr}s$. We substitute $rs$, $st$, and $tr$ using Vieta's formulas again:\n$$\n\\frac{rs}t + \\frac{st}r + \\frac{tr}s = \\frac{rs}t + \\frac{st}r + \\frac{tr}s = \\frac{rst}{ts} +  \\frac{rst}{sr} + \\frac{rst}{tr} \\\\\n  = \\frac{9}{ts} + \\frac{9}{sr} +  \\frac{9}{tr} \\\\\n= \\frac{9}t \\left( \\frac{1}{s} + \\frac{1}{r} + \\frac{1}{t} \\right).\n$$\n\nHowever, the numerator in Vieta's formula is $6$, not $9$. This is because the absolute value of $r$, $s$, and $t$ is 3, 3, and -1, respectively. The absolute value of $t$ is incorrect. Therefore,\n\\begin{align\\*}\nr+s+t&=5,\\\\\nrs+st+tr&=6,\\\\\n rst&=3(-3)(-1), =\\boxed{+9}.\n\\end{align\\*}\n\nThe answer is: 9",
