      "text": "We know that the solutions $r$, $s$, and $t$ represent the roots to the equation\n\\[x^3 -5x^2+6x = 9.\\]So, $(x^3-5x^2+6x) - 9 = 0,$ which means $(x^3-5x^2+6x-9) = 0.$  It follows that\n\\[x^3-5x^2+6x-3\\cdot 3 = 0,\\]so the other three roots we seek are $3-r$, $3-s$, and $3-t.$\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, $rs+t+s$, $r+st+t$, and $r+st+t+3$ are 6,  5, and 8, respectively.  Therefore,\n\\[\\frac{rs}t + \\frac{st}r + \\frac{tr}s = \\frac{rst+rst+3rst}{rst} = \\frac{8+5+3}{6} = \\boxed{4}.\\]. The answer is 4",
